ontent": "Take Away"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment."}]}]}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "id": 0, "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"contents": [{"type": "video", "value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"time": "100", "image": "", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong notdialogue\">A Night in Jail</span><br /><br />I remember the first time I was sent to jail.<br/>\nIt happened on a ski vacation in the mountains with some friends. My uncle's cabin was located not far from the ski hill, and we were allowed to use it for the weekend. After we had unpacked, we went to the village nearby. We got tired and headed back to the cabin."}, {"time": "21500", "image": "", "id": 2, "text": "\u201cWho has the key?\u201d I asked Sandra.<br/>\n\u201cI don't have it,\u201d she said. \u201cMaybe David does.\u201d<br/>\n\u201cI don't have it either,\u201d David said.<br/>\n\u201cUh oh,\u201d I thought. \u201cWhere is the extra key kept?\u201d We had mistakenly locked ourselves out!<br/>\nDavid went around the back of the cabin. \u201cThe key could be hidden somewhere. Let's look,\u201d he said."}, {"time": "42250", "image": "", "id": 3, "text": "The neighbors were watching out for suspicious occurrences from the windows. \u201cMaybe we'll try to break in,\u201d David said. Then, David tried to open the back door with a shovel. He wasn't very successful.<br/>\n\u201cMaybe we should break one of the windows and then it can be replaced before we leave,\u201d I said."}, {"time": "58500", "image": "", "id": 4, "text": "In the meantime, the neighbors had already called the police. When the police car drove up to the house, they caught us breaking and entering. We tried to explain. I told them I was the niece and that we had locked the key inside. They didn't believe us. After a night spent in a holding cell, we managed to get in touch with my uncle. Next time we won't forget the key!"}], "video_src": "engenn8le03ob11re2vid01"}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "video", "id": 2, "_data": []}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Crime and Punishment"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": " A Night in Jail"}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Identify and describe rules and obligations through a wider range of language and expressions in both work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands important and specific information in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Understands important and specific information in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Understands important and specific information in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Understands important and specific information in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Understands important and specific information in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Understands important and specific information in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands important and specific information in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands important and specific information in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn8le03ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " The Past Perfect Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You use the Past Perfect tense to identify and talk about an 'earlier past'."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you are talking about a past event, you can refer to something that happened at an earlier time to that past event by using the Past Perfect tense.<br /><br />  The structure of the Past Perfect is:<br /><br />  Subject + had + past participle<br /><br />   <span class=\"italic\">When I arrived at the party, Vanessa <span class=\"strong\">had</span> already <span class=\"strong\">gone</span> home. </span><br /> Which event happened <span class=\"italic\">first</span>? Vanessa went home.<br /> Which event happened <span class=\"italic\">later</span>? I arrived at the party.<br /><br />  You use the Past Perfect tense (not Simple Past) when you want to talk about how long something had continued <span class=\"strong\">up to a past moment</span>. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Before 2010, the number of home and car break-ins had nearly doubled in the metropolitan area. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "We had feared walking home at night."}, {"type": "example", "content": "\"I'm glad we had started a neighborhood watch program as early as we did.\""}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Simple Past Passive, Simple Passive and Modal Verbs in the Passive Voice"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use an active structure when you want the 'doer' of the action to be the subject.<br /> You use a passive structure when you want the 'receiver' of the action to be the subject. <br /><br />  You use modal verbs (<span class=\"italic\">can, could, may, might, have to</span>) to add meaning to other verbs. They come before the dictionary form (Infinitive without 'to') of the main verb. <br />    Modal verbs can add meaning connected with certainty or obligation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Active sentence = <span class=\"italic\">The prison staff(subject) locked prisoners (object) in their cells at night.</span><br />Passive sentence = <span class=\"italic\">Prisoners (subject)<span class=\"strong\"> were locked </span>in their cells at night (by the prison staff).</span> <br /><br/> It is not necessary to mention the object in a passive sentence. <br /><br />  You make the passive form of a verb by using tenses of the verb to be followed by the past participle. <br /><br />  The Simple Past passive form is:<br /><br />  was/were + past participle<br /><br />  <span class=\"italic\">The building <span class=\"strong\">was built</span> in 1993.</span><br /><br />   The Simple Present passive form is:<br /><br />  am/are/is + past participle<br /><br />  <span class=\"italic\">The key <span class=\"strong\">is kept </span>under the rock.</span><br /><br />  You can add a modal verb before the verb to be.<br /><br />  Subject + modal + To be + past participle<br /><br />  For example:<br /><span class=\"italic\">The key <span class=\"strong\">could be hidden</span> somewhere.</span><br /><br />  Here the sentence now has an additional meaning of possibility, thanks to the modal <span class=\"strong\">could</span>."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I remember the first time I <span class=\"strong\">was sent</span> to jail. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "My uncle's cabin<span class=\"strong\"> was located </span>not far from the ski hill, and we were allowed to use it for the weekend."}, {"type": "example", "content": "\"Maybe we should break one of the windows and then it can <span class=\"strong\">be replaced </span>before we leave,\" I said. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "\u201cWhere is the extra key<span class=\"strong\"> kept</span>?\u201d"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "mistakenly "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "by mistake"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We had mistakenly locked ourselves out! "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le03ob11aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words to review."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "holding cell"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a small room where people wait to have their trial"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: After a night spent in a holding cell, we managed to get in touch with my uncle."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le03ob11aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to watch out for "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to look for"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The neighbors were watching out for strange occurrences from their windows."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le03ob11aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "suspicious "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "causing someone to believe that something is not right"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The neighbors were looking for suspicious activities from their windows."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le03ob11aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "occurrence"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "happening; incident; event "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The neighbors were watching out for suspicious occurrences from their windows."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le03ob11aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "breaking and entering"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the act of illegally opening and entering someone's house"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: When the police car drove up to the house, they caught us breaking and entering."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le03ob11aud06"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write a funny story about someone who was mistakenly send to jail."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Be creative! It doesn't have to be true. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Exchange your story with a partner and correct any errors you find in your partner's writing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your story aloud to your partner or a group."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Which story is the funniest?"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I talk about rules, regulations, crime and punishment."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about what is supposed to happen."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about things I had done or things that had happened."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write creative stories."}]}]}